  "coverage_notes": [
    "Surface-web engines expose different indexes and result-provider mixes.",
    "Metasearch engines add provider diversity but do not create a universal index.",
    "Scholarly and repository indexes are specialized deep-web discovery surfaces rather than general dark-web engines.",
    "Tor onion search indexes are partial and volatile; an onion service for a surface-web engine is not equivalent to a comprehensive dark-web index.",
    "Authenticated, closed-community, and private databases remain separate deep-web access planes and require authorized imports or direct authenticated access."
